description:
Implement a 4-to-1 multiplexer circuit. It takes four input signals (in0, in1, in2, in3) and a 2-bit select signal (sel) to choose one of the inputs to output. The module uses two levels of 2-to-1 multiplexers to first select between pairs of inputs and then combine those results to provide a single output based on the select signal's value.
module top_module(
  output reg out,
  input [3:0] in0, in1, in2, in3,
  input [1:0] sel
);

code:
module top_module(
  output reg out,
  input [3:0] in0, in1, in2, in3,
  input [1:0] sel
);always @(*) begin
    case (sel)
      2'b00: out = in0;
      2'b01: out = in1;
      2'b10: out = in2;
      2'b11: out = in3;
      default: out = 1'b0; // Default case to avoid latches
    endcase
  end

endmodule

